## 6) Configured npm scripts
- `build`: `npm run build:renderer && tsup && node scripts/copy-renderer.mjs`
- `build:renderer`: `vite build --config src/renderer/vite.config.mjs`
- `dev`: `concurrently -k -n renderer,electron -c cyan,green "npm run dev:renderer" "npm run dev:electron"`
- `dev:renderer`: `vite --config src/renderer/vite.config.mjs`
- `dev:electron`: `wait-on tcp:5173 && cross-env NODE_ENV=dev NODE_OPTIONS=--import=tsx electron --no-sandbox --disable-setuid-sandbox src/main.ts`
- `lint`: `eslint .`
- `lint:fix`: `eslint . --fix`
- `format`: `prettier . --write`
- `format:check`: `prettier . --check`
- `postinstall`: `npm run rebuild:electron`
- `start`: `electron --no-sandbox --disable-setuid-sandbox dist/fortuna.js`
- `rebuild:electron`: `electron-rebuild -f -w better-sqlite3`
- `check`: `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`

## 7) TypeScript configuration (tsconfig)
- Modern ECMAScript target: `target: ESNext`
- Modern library set: `lib: ["ESNext"]`
- Node module format: `module: ESNext`
- Module resolution: `moduleResolution: Bundler`
- Paths alias:
  - `@db` -> `./src/database/index.ts`
- Strict mode enabled: `strict: true`
- Additional safety flags:
  - `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
  - `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`
  - `isolatedModules`
  - `verbatimModuleSyntax`
- Local TypeScript imports are written without `.js` extension (e.g., `./database`, `./client`, `./schema`).
- Artifact generation:
  - `declaration: true`
  - `declarationMap: true`
  - `sourceMap: true`
- Directories:
  - input: `src/`
  - output: `dist/`

## 8) Known notes
- npm distribution build:
- Entry: `src/main.ts`
- Single output file: `dist/fortuna.js`
- Minification: enabled
- Sourcemap: disabled
- Build also copies `src/renderer/index.html` to `dist/index.html`.
- Build copies all renderer build assets from `src/renderer/dist` to root `dist`.
- `npm run dev` starts Vite first and then Electron.
- Dev TypeScript loading is done via `NODE_OPTIONS='--import tsx'`.
- In dev (`NODE_ENV=dev`), Electron loads `http://localhost:5173`.
- `npm run start` opens Electron using built files in root `dist/` (`fortuna.js` + Vite output).
- Vite renderer uses `base: './'` so built asset paths work under Electron `file://` on `npm run start`.
- In Linux environments without configured `chrome-sandbox` SUID, dev/start run with `--no-sandbox --disable-setuid-sandbox`.
- `better-sqlite3` must be rebuilt for Electron ABI (`npm run rebuild:electron`) after install/version changes.
- Rebuild is automated on install via `postinstall`.
- Electron was bumped to a secure major version line to address `npm audit` high-severity advisories.
- Database path resolution by `NODE_ENV`:
- `dev`: `path.join(process.cwd(), 'dev.db')`
- default (no `NODE_ENV=dev`): `~/.fortuna/fortuna.db` (directory is created automatically)
- Migrations:
- `migrations` table is always created as prerequisite (not versioned migration).
- Tracks `version`, `name`, and `executed_at`.
- Supports automatic `up` and `down` synchronization based on numeric version comparison between DB and migration files.
- If DB version is lower than the latest migration file version, pending `up` migrations are applied automatically.
- If DB version is higher than the latest migration file version, `down` is applied automatically until synchronization.
- If a DB-applied version no longer has a migration file, its registry row is removed from `migrations` to allow auto-sync with current code state.
- Current versioned migration:
- `v1` (`create_types_table`) creates table `types` with:
  - `id` generated (`integer primary key autoincrement`)
  - `group` (`text`)
  - `value` (`text`)
- Database lifecycle:
- instance is created lazily via `getDb()` and reused (single process instance)
- app quit is intercepted in `before-quit` to await `destroyDb()` before final shutdown
- Schema pattern:
- all DB schemas are split inside `src/database/schema/*` and composed in `src/database/schema/index.ts`.
- with `verbatimModuleSyntax`, type-only re-exports must use `export type`.
- Lint and format should run before npm publish.
- Type-aware ESLint uses `tsconfig.eslint.json` to avoid files outside `rootDir` from `tsconfig.json`.
- Current Prettier rules:
- `singleQuote: true`
- `trailingComma: "all"`
- `semi: true`
- `printWidth: 100`
- `tabWidth: 2`
- Import order is enforced automatically by ESLint (`simple-import-sort`) and can be fixed with `npm run lint:fix`.

## 9) Conventions for next changes
- Keep TypeScript sources in `src/` and build output in `dist/`.
- Prefer modern configuration (`ESNext`) unless compatibility requires otherwise.
- Mandatory rule: always update this file (`.codex`) whenever architecture, scripts, tooling, folder structure, or build/runtime flow changes.
- Mandatory rule: after any code change, always run `npm run lint:fix`.

## 10) Collaboration flow (terminal)
- Agreed flow:
- The user runs only installation commands when requested (`npm install`, `npm i`, `npm install -D`, etc.).
- The agent performs all other configuration and file changes directly in the project.
